{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971450-bringing-the-dark-mechanical-into-awakening","id":971450,"title":"Bringing the Dark Mechanical into Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T12:20:10-07:00","id":971450,"title":"Bringing the Dark Mechanical into Awakening","content":"This isn't another &quot;Mages and the Machine&quot; thread, as interesting as those are, though that might be part of it. I'm wondering how to weird science up Mage. Not just making it possible to play a mad scientist, but enriching the Fallen World with the postmodern Dark Mechanical aesthetic of Genius (which bears a striking resemblance to GMC and Demon). What sorts of hacks and reflavoring capture the feeling of Mages as burning spanners tossed into a vast and terrifying mechanical ecosystem? One of the subthemes of Genius, which I always loved, was the idea that humans aren't really in control of technology, that it's effectively another dimension of nature, and that humans ultimately have to change themselves to adapt to technology rather than technology changing for them. The merits of that idea aside, it's certainly effective for a horror story. <br /> <br /> Another idea- making an ST decision that reckless Time magic has a high chance of attracting GM/Time Hunter attention (hey, it needs a nerf). Actually, building up a Mages vs. Machine conflict gets a lot of atmosphere from Genius in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:31:04-07:00","id":972342,"title":"","content":"The idea that humanity adapts itself to fill the needs of technology is straight out of Upton Sinclair, just recasting industry to resemble the way it was at the turn of the 19th century and blaming it on the God Machine with the Robber Barons and Captains of Industry being Angels would go a long way to creating the flavor of such a conflict where Mages and their magic are instead totally independent of the God Machine's technology.<br /> \u200bOne idea I played with involved Banishers, instead of Awakenings gone wrong I had the idea that their awakenings were caused by a build up of Paradox (which was actually the system's resistance to magic making changes, not the Abyss) and that the tower they signed was a clock tower that represented the God Machine, awakening in them a calling to use their own god given powers to root out the unholy witches. The Banishers would in many ways become the Technocrancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}